.Dd July 9, 2026
.Dt SCLR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sclr
.Nd drive a spec through a collab, lore, and report process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar spec.org
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a deterministic harness around a single model inference.
Given the path to a
.Ar spec.org
brief, it drives a model through a fixed four-file process, leaving
the deliverables in the spec's own directory.
.Pp
The process is defined by
.Pa agent.org ,
which
.Nm
feeds to the model together with the
.Ar spec.org
path.
The model reads the spec and writes its outputs,
.Pa collab.org ,
.Pa lore.org ,
and
.Pa report.org
\(em each only when it has content \(em as siblings of the spec.
.Nm
passes the spec
.Em path ,
not its contents, because the deliverables are files the model must
create at known locations.
.Pp
.Nm
owns everything around the inference: the argument, the invocation,
and the post-condition.
A finished run leaves a non-empty
.Pa report.org ;
a run blocked on a question leaves a non-empty
.Pa collab.org .
If neither is present when the model returns,
.Nm
reports that nothing useful was produced and fails.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width MODEL
.It Ev MODEL
The model command, defaulting to
.Ql claude .
It is left unquoted at the call site, so additional words split into
separate arguments.
Because the model must be allowed to write files, invoke it with a
permission mode that permits edits:
.Pp
.Dl MODEL="claude --permission-mode acceptEdits" sclr spec.org
.El
.Sh FILES
Relative to the directory holding the
.Ar spec.org :
.Bl -tag -width report.org
.It Pa spec.org
The brief, authored by the user;
.Nm
does not modify it.
.It Pa collab.org
A two-way buffer of questions and answers; present when the run is
blocked.
.It Pa lore.org
Durable facts and decisions, each with the reason it holds.
.It Pa report.org
A concise account of the result; present when the run finished.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the model leaves a non-empty
.Pa report.org
or
.Pa collab.org
beside the spec.
It exits 64 when invoked with no
.Ar spec.org
argument, and 1 when the spec does not exist, the model invocation
fails, or the model returns without producing a deliverable.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Drive a spec to a result, allowing the model to write its
deliverables:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
MODEL="claude --permission-mode acceptEdits" sclr path/to/spec.org
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr hello-model 1
